 get  into school here and I applied at the  very late at a part of the first season  and I'm here now very grateful for that  and the other thing I would say as a  recommendation is really hone your story  GSB is really about stories and if you  don't have your story really tight about  what makes you special and different  it's gonna be hard to get in here  totally agree on that point and for me  my piece of advice on honing your story  is to start early ideally you'll take  plenty of time to really craft those  essays in particular to give the most  authentic picture of you that you can  and don't write the essays thinking that  you have to appear as this incredibly  like superhero type person be authentic  and be you and show what you've truly  done through your stories and your  experiences that makes you  differentiated and unique and if you  focus more on just being true to  yourself and let that come through I  think you'll find great success and  hopefully find yourself among the next  year's crop of applicants or whenever  you come to the GSB alright thank you so  much to Sara and Vinnie if you'd like  there are a tremendous amount of  resources and points of contact  available for you on the GSB Veterans  Club website just Google that it'll come  right up there's also a contact form out  there if you'd like to try and get in  touch with any member the Veterans Club  we're here as a resource to help you and  if we don't know the answer to a  particular question we can definitely  put you in touch with someone who does  know the answer so with that would like  to say thanks so much for joining us  today it's our absolute pleasure to  speak with you good luck and we hope to  see you all soon thank you  you  [Music]  you


